Package: whitecube-desktop
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: Whitecube <whitecube@localhost>
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: fnott, ufw, pipewire, wireplumber, pipewire-pulse, qemu-system-x86, qemu-system-gui, ovmf
Suggests: python3-torch, alsa-utils, chrony, console-setup, systemd-container, qemu-utils, wl-clipboard
Description: Whitecube - Wayland desktop with native image and model training studios
 A compositor (whitecube), top bar (cube-status), settings, living cube wallpaper (cube-ca),
 a native Wi-Fi controller (cube-net), a workspace suite and small apps.
 The net-off and net-on commands provide a reversible IPv4/IPv6 lockdown,
 preserving the existing firewall and local loopback services.
 Cube Editor adds a GTK4 workspace for inspecting, extracting, customizing and
 rebuilding Linux ISO images, with project recipes, build reports and optional
 QEMU testing. System image changes run through an explicit privileged worker.
 Cube Chrootables manages Debian chroot workspaces: debootstrap images with profiles,
 persistent or disposable sessions, snapshots, clones, exports and imports, from a
 Qt window or the whitecube-chrootable-manager command line.
 The wc-* command suite (start with wc-help) opens apps and reports or changes audio,
 network, power and system state from a terminal, with shell completions.
 Cube Strap builds Debian whitecubes with a bundled deb-strap: chroot workspaces
 imported into Chrootables, or bootable UEFI virtual machines added to the whitecube
 image store and run in QEMU.
 Cube Browser is a native Wayland web preview with its own HTML/CSS engine,
 sandboxed renderer and network workers. Cube Player plays films and music
 through libmpv in a native Wayland window.
 Whitecube Trainer adds a native GTK4 workspace for local 1M, 2M, 5M and 10M
 language models, with resumable training, checkpoint previews and Desktop Chat
 integration. Training uses a configured PyTorch environment; the complete model
 pipeline is included. Existing CUDA environments can be reused.
 .
 Everything is installed system-wide. Each account keeps only its own settings, in ~/.config/whitecube
 and the usual dotfiles; /etc/skel carries the defaults for new accounts.
 .
 X-free wlroots and cairo are bundled in /usr/lib/whitecube for the native compositor
 and desktop panels. GTK applications use their own distribution runtime libraries.
 Desktop Chat includes a private Electron runtime and runs through Ozone Wayland.
 Starts from the "Whitecube" Wayland session entry, or from a tty with: exec whitecube-session
